;; The assign-once FIELD-number registry for the minted messages.
;;
;; APPEND-ONLY, AND A PIN IS PERMANENT. An entry here is a wire contract: it
;; survives the field being deleted, precisely so the number can never be
;; handed to a different field later. Deleting a pin frees a number for reuse,
;; which is the one edit that can break a peer that is already deployed.
;;
;; Grown by `protocol-gen reconcile`, never by generating — a generator that
;; could grow its own registry would assign a number as a side effect of being
;; run.
;;
;; ONLY MESSAGES APPEAR HERE. A minted ENUM carries its members' numbers in the
;; mint itself and is skipped by `reconcile` outright, because an empty entry
;; under an enum's id would read exactly like a message whose fields had all
;; been retired.
;;
;; `pgfix.Notice`'s pins are deliberately non-contiguous and disagree with the
;; order its fields are declared in: `level` is declared first and pinned 15,
;; `text` second and pinned 7, `code` third and pinned 4. A generator numbering
;; by position would emit 1/2/3, and the oneof block would list `text` before
;; `code` instead of after it.
{"pgfix.Heartbeat" {"seq" 1, "sent_at_ns" 2}
 "pgfix.Notice" {"code" 4, "level" 15, "text" 7}}
